{#-
Selects the pre-baked lock for this render and stamps the project name into it.

The files under `locks/` are real uv.lock artifacts: byte-for-byte what `uv lock`
wrote against this template's rendered pyproject.toml, holding no jinja at all.
That is deliberate. uv can validate one, `tomllib` can parse one, cve-sync gates
them where they sit, and an SCA scanner recognises them by name and path instead
of skipping an opaque `.j2`. They are excluded from the copy in `copier.yml`, so
only the one selected here reaches a rendered project.

The single thing that cannot be baked in is the project name, because it is the
customer's choice. Each lock therefore carries the literal placeholder
`af-agent-placeholder` and the swap happens below, as a value substitution rather
than a jinja tag living inside the artifact.

`agent_app_name` is normalised the way uv normalises `[project].name` when it
writes a lock (PEP 503: lowercased, `_` to `-`), so the emitted line is what a
customer running `uv lock` themselves would produce and never shows up as a diff.
uv compares this name normalised, so an app name that normalises imperfectly
(`a__b`) is still accepted rather than failing `uv lock --check`.

One lock exists per *distinct resolution*, which is fewer than one per framework:

  - `nat` resolves identically to `base`. Both render
    `datarobot-genai[dragent, auth]`, and the nat entry point is metadata, not a
    dependency, so uv produces the same graph.
  - The memory providers add no dependencies at all. `pyproject.toml.jinja` has no
    `use_agent_memory` conditional, and `mem0ai` already arrives transitively
    through datarobot-genai.

Both used to have a lock of their own. Because `uv lock --check` only asks whether
a lock satisfies its pyproject, and a copy always does, the copies drifted
unnoticed: the memory lock shipped a wcwidth a release behind base for months.
Sharing one file makes that class of drift impossible rather than merely unlikely.
Do not add a lock for a variant until its dependency graph actually differs.

Regenerate with `task update-lock-file AGENT=<variant>`, never by hand.
See docs/development.md.
-#}
{%- set LOCK_VARIANTS = ['crewai', 'langgraph', 'llamaindex'] -%}
{%- set lock_variant = agent_template_framework if agent_template_framework in LOCK_VARIANTS else 'base' -%}
{%- set project_name = agent_app_name | lower | replace('_', '-') -%}
{%- filter replace('name = "af-agent-placeholder"', 'name = "' ~ project_name ~ '"') -%}
{%- include 'template/{{agent_app_name}}/locks/' ~ lock_variant ~ '/uv.lock' -%}
{%- endfilter -%}
